# The build context is the repository root, and almost none of it belongs in
# the image.

.git
.githooks
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc

# Virtualenvs are build artifacts: the image makes its own, and a host venv
# points at interpreters that do not exist inside it.
**/venv
**/.venv

# Confidential data and models. DATA/ is a read-only MOUNT at runtime, never
# a layer -- an image is copied around, a mount is not.
DATA

# The in-process tools are SHIPPED, and the exclusion that used to sit here is
# gone with its reason. It read "importing these would need the very stack the
# API venv is built without", which was true when server/tools/ held AMASSS,
# ALI and ASO; what is left is 48 kB importing `base` and `file_utils` and
# nothing else.
#
# They earn their place: `Test_Tool` takes two strings and returns their
# concatenation, so a fresh deployment can prove its whole round trip -- auth,
# upload, run, result -- before a single model has been downloaded, which
# nothing else here can do. `Example_Tool` is the panel showcase the client's
# ExampleTool module renders.
#
# Their virtualenvs and caches are still excluded, by the **/venv rules above.

# Not the server's business.
server/tests
docker/fixtures
scripts
*.md
